            <ArticleTitle>Chronic groin pain in an athlete: an unusual presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persistent disabling groin pain in an active sportsman is a frustrating diagnostic and management problem for both the athlete and physician. After clinical examination and investigation there remains a group of patients who have unexplained groin pain, and may undergo lengthy periods of conservative management with numerous radiological investigations. Here we highlight such a case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
